%% Bootstrap Deployment Flow - Sequence Diagram

sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant GUI as GUI Installer
    participant FS as File System
    participant Val as Validator
    participant Win as Windows Scripts
    participant WSL as WSL Scripts
    participant PC as Target PC

    Note over User,PC: Phase 1: Selection & Validation
    User->>GUI: Select PC (e.g., worker-rtx3060)
    GUI->>FS: Load manifests/*.yaml
    FS-->>GUI: PC configuration

    User->>GUI: Select components
    GUI->>GUI: Build component list

    User->>GUI: Click "Install"
    GUI->>Val: Validate prerequisites
    Val->>PC: Check disk space, RAM, etc.
    PC-->>Val: System info
    Val-->>GUI: Validation result

    alt Validation Failed
        GUI->>User: Show errors, abort
    end

    Note over User,PC: Phase 2: Backup
    GUI->>FS: Backup existing configs
    FS-->>GUI: Backup complete

    Note over User,PC: Phase 3: Windows Bootstrap
    loop For each component
        GUI->>FS: Load scripts/components/windows/{component}.ps1
        GUI->>Win: Execute PowerShell script
        Win->>PC: Install component
        PC-->>Win: Installation result
        Win-->>GUI: Success/Failure
        GUI->>User: Update progress bar
    end

    Note over User,PC: Phase 4: WSL Bootstrap (if required)
    alt PC has WSL
        loop For each component
            GUI->>FS: Load scripts/components/wsl/{component}.sh
            GUI->>WSL: Execute Bash script
            WSL->>PC: Install component in WSL
            PC-->>WSL: Installation result
            WSL-->>GUI: Success/Failure
            GUI->>User: Update progress bar
        end
    end

    Note over User,PC: Phase 5: Config Deployment
    loop For each component config
        GUI->>FS: Load configs/{component}/*
        GUI->>GUI: Inject PC-specific variables
        GUI->>PC: Deploy config file
        PC-->>GUI: Deployment result
        GUI->>User: Update progress bar
    end

    Note over User,PC: Phase 6: Post-Validation
    GUI->>PC: Run smoke tests
    PC-->>GUI: Test results

    alt Tests Failed
        GUI->>User: Show errors
        User->>GUI: Rollback?
        alt User confirms rollback
            GUI->>PC: Restore backups
            PC-->>GUI: Rollback complete
            GUI->>User: Installation rolled back
        end
    else Tests Passed
        GUI->>User: Installation complete!
    end
